# Accepted-risk misconfigs in terraform/modules/vpc, all intentional design
# choices rather than oversights. Decision: Step 8.3 CI wiring surfaced these
# for the first time (trivy was never run against this module before), so they
# were never actually fixed - just never checked. Review by the exp: date.
#
# AVD-AWS-0104: EKS node security group egress is 0.0.0.0/0. Nodes need
# outbound access to ECR, GitHub, and EKS add-on endpoints; those IP ranges
# change and aren't practical to pin. Egress-only, no inbound exposure.
#
# AVD-AWS-0164: public subnets auto-assign public IPs. That's the definition
# of a public subnet in this design - the ALB lives here.
#
# AVD-AWS-0017: VPC flow-log CloudWatch group isn't KMS-encrypted. Genuinely
# fixable (add a CMK), just out of scope for CI plumbing - tracked for the
# Phase 10 security hardening pass instead of bundled into this PR.
AVD-AWS-0104 exp:2027-02-28
AVD-AWS-0164 exp:2027-02-28
AVD-AWS-0017 exp:2027-02-28
